        "Fine-Tuning a Small Language Model Using LoRA on a Custom Question-Answer Dataset\n",
        "1. Introduction\n",
        "Large Language Models (LLMs) are capable of understanding and generating human-like text. However, adapting a pre-trained language model to a specific domain or task can require significant computational resources.\n",
        "\n",
        "Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning (PEFT) provides a solution by updating only a small portion of the model's parameters. In this project, Low-Rank Adaptation (LoRA) is used to fine-tune Microsoft's Phi-2 language model on a custom Question-Answer dataset.\n",
        "\n",
